2. ABOUT THE BEST OF EDO AWARD

Who We Are

The Prestigious Best of Edo Award is an annual recognition platform dedicated to celebrating exceptional sons, daughters and friends of Edo State whose achievements and contributions have created meaningful impact across different sectors of society.

The Award recognises excellence across fields including leadership and public service, business and entrepreneurship, education, healthcare, media and communication, arts, culture and entertainment, innovation and technology, and new media.

Our purpose goes beyond presenting trophies. We seek to create a lasting culture in which achievement is recognised, positive stories are amplified, outstanding role models are celebrated, and younger generations are inspired to pursue excellence.

Our Philosophy

We believe that every society has individuals whose contributions deserve to be recognised and preserved.

Behind every successful business, transformative institution, creative achievement, community contribution or professional accomplishment is a story of determination, sacrifice, courage and vision.

The Best of Edo Award provides a platform for those stories to be told.

We believe recognition should not be based solely on popularity, wealth or public visibility. It should be rooted in achievement, character, contribution, impact, innovation, leadership and service.

Inspired by Edo Heritage

The identity of the Best of Edo Award is deeply connected to the heritage of the Edo people.

The historic Benin Kingdom is recognised for its sophisticated traditions of governance, artistry, craftsmanship, diplomacy and cultural expression. Its artistic and cultural legacy continues to command international attention and remains an important part of the story of Edo.

The Best of Edo Award draws inspiration from this heritage—not simply to celebrate the past, but to encourage a new generation to build upon it.

Our objective is to connect the enduring values associated with Edo heritage with contemporary achievement in business, leadership, science, technology, education, healthcare, media, entertainment and other fields.

What We Do

Through our annual award programme and associated initiatives, we:

- Identify deserving individuals and organisations.
- Celebrate outstanding achievements and contributions.
- Give visibility to inspiring stories and accomplishments.
- Promote positive narratives about Edo State and its people.
- Encourage younger generations to pursue excellence.
- Create opportunities for networking and collaboration.
- Promote Edo culture, identity and heritage.
- Support conversations around leadership, innovation and development.
- Encourage social responsibility and humanitarian engagement.
- Preserve the stories and legacies of people who have made meaningful contributions.

More Than an Annual Ceremony

The Best of Edo Award is designed to exist beyond the night of the award ceremony.

It serves as a meeting point for achievers, professionals, entrepreneurs, creatives, leaders, institutions, young people, partners and members of the wider Edo community.

Through recognition, engagement, media visibility, partnerships and social-impact initiatives, the platform seeks to build an ecosystem where excellence is not only celebrated but also encouraged to multiply.

Our Growing Journey

From its earlier editions to the present, the Best of Edo Award has continued to develop as a platform for celebrating achievement and Edo identity.

The 9th Edition of the Prestigious Best of Edo Award 2026 represents another important chapter in that journey, reflecting the organisation's continuing commitment to excellence, heritage, visibility and impact.

As the platform grows, its fundamental principle remains unchanged:

To recognise people who are making a difference and inspire others to do the same.

Our Promise

We will continue to tell the stories of achievement with dignity, celebrate deserving people with purpose, uphold the values of excellence and integrity, and create a platform that future generations can look back on with pride.

The Best of Edo Award is a celebration of who we are, what we have achieved, and what we can become.






3. OUR HISTORY

FROM EDO HERITAGE TO GLOBAL RECOGNITION

The story of the Best of Edo Award is closely connected to a broader story—the story of a people whose history, culture, creativity, enterprise and achievements have continued to command attention beyond their immediate homeland.

Edo State occupies an important place in Nigeria's cultural history. At the heart of this heritage is the historic Benin Kingdom, renowned for its sophisticated traditions, artistic achievements, craftsmanship, leadership and cultural institutions.

For generations, Edo people have contributed significantly to Nigeria's development and have distinguished themselves across business, politics, education, medicine, entertainment, the arts, technology, professional practice and other fields.

The Best of Edo Award was conceived within this tradition of excellence: to create a platform through which outstanding contemporary achievements could be identified, celebrated and documented.

THE BEGINNING OF A JOURNEY

The Best of Edo Award has evolved through successive editions, growing from an award initiative into a broader platform for recognition, visibility, networking and social impact.

By its 7th Edition in 2024, the Award had established a significant history of celebrating distinguished individuals and contributors connected to Edo State.

The subsequent editions continued that journey, providing opportunities to recognise people whose achievements have contributed to the growth, development and positive image of Edo State and Nigeria.

The platform has continued to evolve with changing times while retaining its central purpose: to recognise excellence and inspire greater impact.

BUILDING A LEGACY OF RECOGNITION

Every edition of the Best of Edo Award adds another chapter to its institutional story.

The Award has sought to bring together accomplished personalities, professionals, entrepreneurs, creatives, public figures, institutions, young people, media organisations, partners and members of the wider community.

Through these engagements, the platform seeks to achieve something beyond the presentation of awards: to create a record of achievement that can inspire generations yet unborn.

Recognition creates memory.

When the story of an achiever is documented and celebrated, that story becomes part of the collective history of the society.

This is one of the reasons the Best of Edo Award places importance on documenting its recipients and their contributions.

FROM LOCAL PRIDE TO GLOBAL OUTLOOK

Edo identity is not confined by geography.

Edo people and people of Edo heritage can be found across Nigeria and around the world, contributing to different sectors and communities.

The Best of Edo Award therefore looks beyond geographical boundaries.

Its vision is to create a bridge between Edo heritage and global achievement—recognising people whose work demonstrates that excellence rooted in Edo can have significance far beyond Edo State.

The Award seeks to contribute to a positive global narrative about Edo people: one centred on achievement, creativity, leadership, resilience, enterprise, culture and service.

THE 9TH EDITION: A NEW CHAPTER

The 9th Edition of the Prestigious Best of Edo Award 2026, scheduled for Sunday, 15 November 2026, in Benin City, Edo State, represents another milestone in the continuing journey of the platform.

This edition builds on the experiences and lessons of previous years while expanding the Award's focus on recognition, partnerships, visibility, heritage and social impact.

It is a celebration of today's achievers and, equally, an investment in tomorrow's possibilities.

PRESERVING THE PAST. CELEBRATING THE PRESENT. INSPIRING THE FUTURE.

The history of the Best of Edo Award is still being written.

Every nominee, recipient, partner, volunteer, sponsor, media organisation and supporter contributes a chapter to that story.

As the platform moves forward, its commitment remains to preserve the values that have shaped Edo identity while celebrating the people who are shaping its future.

Our past gives us identity.
